  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 accuracy. The image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality contributes limited signal. This raises the question of whether concat fusion (which treats both modalities symmetrically) is optimal, or whether weighted fusion could let the model adaptively down-weight the weaker image signal and lean more on the strong RNA representation. config_033 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while holding all other settings identical to the current best, providing a clean single-variable comparison. Under the tight budget of 2 remaining experiments, isolating the fusion effect is the highest-value next step: if weighted fusion improves accuracy, it establishes a stronger base for the final experiments; if not, it confirms concat is sufficient and frees the remaining budget to test alternative image encoders (e.g., imagenet_vit_l) or other extensions."
}

